WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.358
Running Learn's definition
against the fakes

2
00:00:02.358 --> 00:00:04.787
shows what it gets right
and what it leaves to you.

3
00:00:04.787 --> 00:00:07.277
It gets the identity right: no secret,

4
00:00:07.277 --> 00:00:11.675
just the Logic App's managed
identity, and the program keeps that.

5
00:00:11.675 --> 00:00:17.195
But the callback is hard-wired to the
worldwide cloud and the beta endpoint,

6
00:00:17.195 --> 00:00:20.400
so in GCC High or DoD it
simply never arrives.

7
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.621
It trusts whatever path it's handed,

8
00:00:22.621 --> 00:00:27.062
which means a forged payload could
aim that identity's token anywhere.

9
00:00:27.062 --> 00:00:31.287
And it always says the work completed,
even when the revocation failed.

10
00:00:31.287 --> 00:00:34.200
Each of those has a fix, pinned by a test.
